{"results":[{"url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/scf/dataviz/scf/table/","final_url":"https://www.federalreserve.gov/econres/scf/dataviz/scf/table/","title":"The Fed - Table: Survey of Consumer Finances, 1989 - 2025","description":"The Federal Reserve Board of Governors in Washington DC.","language":"en","text":"## Survey of Consumer Finances (SCF)\n\nShare\n\n\nFull CSV\n\n### Survey of Consumer Finances, 1989 - 2025\n\n#### Before-tax family income by all families\n\nMake Full Screen\n\n| Date | All families (US$ Thousands) |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1989 | 65.81 |\n| 1992 | 60.42 |\n| 1995 | 65.08 |\n| 1998 | 66.74 |\n| 2001 | 73.49 |\n| 2004 | 74.15 |\n| 2007 | 74.08 |\n| 2010 | 68.35 |\n| 2013 | 65.05 |\n| 2016 | 71.10 |\n| 2019 | 74.91 |\n| 2022 | 76.89 |\n| 2025 | 82.16 |\n\n***Note:**\nThe income, asset, and liability data used to make these charts are the public versions of those used in this\narticle, and were created using this\nprogram.\nThe article and program also contain variable definitions.\nFor more information on how the asset, debt, and net worth variables are related, please consult this\nflowchart.\nFor each variable and classification group, the charts show the percent of families in the group who have the item,\nand the median and mean amounts of holdings for those who have any. Two exceptions to this are that all households\nare included in the net worth and income measures. Users should be aware that unlike the tables published in the\nBulletin article, the charts include estimates for cells with fewer than eleven observations, a sample size deemed\ninsufficient for robust estimates (see tables to identify which variables and groups are affected).\nAll dollar estimates are given in 2025 dollars.*\n\nOn September 28, 2020 the drop down for \"Distributed by\" was updated from \"head\" to \"reference person\" to be consistent with SCF tables and bulletin article.\n\nOn October 18, 2023, the data visualizations were updated to correct a data labelling issue.\n\nOn November 2, 2023, the data visualizations were updated to correct a display issue with percent holdings.\n\n*Data visualization disclaimer*\n\nLast Update: October 09, 2026","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":1384.9370799944154,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}